    "rich_text_KckTAy": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_fqNbJU": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Is OSHA Compliance Crucial?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_i3qdf3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>OSHA’s promotion of a healthy and safe work environment is essential to a functioning workplace. They are a source of education, training, assistance, and outreach for employees and employers. OSHA also enforces standards for workplace safety that employers must follow.</p><p>Employers must maintain a workplace where serious hazards are not present under the General Duty Clause stated under the Occupational Safety and Health (OSH) Act. Employees have the right to work in a safe environment. The OSH Act was signed into law in 1970 to prevent the severe harm and death of employees while working. Employers must provide working conditions where known and recognized dangers are not present under federal law.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_fqNbJU",
        "text_i3qdf3"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich-text.name",
      "settings": {
        "container": "fixed",
        "color_scheme": "",
        "use_color_scheme_in_container": false,
        "content_spacing": "standard",
        "content_alignment": "left",
        "padding_top": 0,
