      }
    },
    "image_with_text_LDCpPz": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_zQYxJC": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What Are the Various Adhesive Tapes and Labels Used for OSHA Worker Health and Safety?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_zrLgKm": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Adhesive tapes and labels are vital to maintaining OSHA workplace standards. NADCO custom prints the following adhesive tapes and labels to promote OSHA workplace standards:</p><ul><li><strong>Highway Reflective Tape</strong>. This type of tape is worn by employees to improve nighttime and low-light visibility. The tape reflects light to the driver’s eyes when an automobile headlight or another light source illuminates the reflective surface. It guarantees higher visibility for safety during an emergency when lighting conditions are poor.</li><li><a href=\"https://shopnadco.com/pages/safety-tapes\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://shopnadco.com/pages/safety-tapes\"><strong>Anti-Slip Tape</strong></a>. Anti-slip tape offers a physical slip prevention measure for ramps, decks, ladders, bathtubs, and other accident-prone areas. NADCO relies on materials with high longevity that exceed several OSHA standards for anti-slip tape. Our anti-slip tape comes in various styles, for use in boats, houses, and buildings.</li><li><a href=\"/pages/social-distancing-decals\" title=\"Social Distancing Decals & Tapes\"><strong>Social Distancing Tape</strong></a>. Social distancing tape provides a clear visual boundary to help customers practice social distancing without confusion. We use eye-catching bold colors and designs to ensure customers are immediately aware that social distancing guidelines are in place.</li><li><strong>Department of Transportation (DOT) Hazard Warning Labels</strong>. These types of labels are used on trucks and vessels to warn that they are containing or transporting hazardous chemicals, flammable liquids, and other dangerous cargo.</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_zQYxJC",
        "text_zrLgKm"
      ],
